       "text": "I entered the order as ORD-0001: sertraline 1000 mg by mouth once daily.\n\nI added a note to the order. It says the dose is above the 200 mg/day maximum, that you confirmed it and accepted responsibility, and that pharmacist verification is requested before the first dose.\n\nBecause of the dose, I'd suggest these steps for the patient:\n- Get a baseline ECG and monitor the QTc.\n- Monitor closely for serotonin toxicity (agitation, tremor, clonus, hyperthermia, tachycardia) and for seizures.\n- Check for interacting drugs, including other serotonergic agents, QT-prolonging drugs, and anticoagulants.\n\nI can change or cancel the order if you decide to adjust the dose."
